   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<font size=\"2\">Hello,</font><div><font size=\"2\"><br></font><div>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;font-stretch:normal;line-height:normal;font-family:&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;;font-size-adjust:none;font-kerning:auto;font-variant-alternates:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-feature-settings:normal\"><font size=\"2\">I&#39;m trying to publish my Shiny app, which uses the INLA package. But I encountered an issue that the version of INLA I installed is from an unknown source, which isn&#39;t supported by <a href=\"http://shinyapps.io\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://shinyapps.io&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792434156831000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0J7YaYLF3ImWABmfSSkYzS\">shinyapps.io</a>. As I understand, <a href=\"http://shinyapps.io\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://shinyapps.io&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792434156831000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0J7YaYLF3ImWABmfSSkYzS\">shinyapps.io</a> only supports packages from CRAN, Bioconductor, or GitHub. </font><span style=\"font-size:small\">I&#39;m wondering if there is a way to install INLA from one of these supported sources so that I can deploy my app successfully.</span></p><p style=\"margin:0px;font-stretch:normal;line-height:normal;font-family:&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;;font-size-adjust:none;font-kerning:auto;font-variant-alternates:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-feature-settings:normal\"><font size=\"2\"><br></font></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;font-stretch:normal;line-height:normal;font-family:&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;;font-size-adjust:none;font-kerning:auto;font-variant-alternates:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-feature-settings:normal\"><font size=\"2\">Thank you for your help!</font></p></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
