   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi,<div><a href=\"http://shinyapps.io\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://shinyapps.io&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792434156832000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3_ku2PC_KOEx64DiPk5kx5\">shinyapps.io</a> has been a notoriously difficult problem, and I&#39;m not aware of any solution (except to develop a fully integrated binary build system that can build the INLA binaries as part of the R package build process, without manual intervention; this does not currently exist).<br>I know some people who said they gave up on <a href=\"http://shinyapps.io\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://shinyapps.io&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792434156832000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3_ku2PC_KOEx64DiPk5kx5\">shinyapps.io</a> for INLA and used Posit Connect instead (but I don&#39;t know anything about how that works and if it can be used in the same way).</div><div>Finn</div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
